[0.001, "o", "5;139;107mUndulating…\\u001b[39m\\u001b[40;1H\\u001b[38;3H\\u001b[?25\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m       +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mh\\u001b[?2026l\"]                                                                                                                                  \r\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m  ⎿  \u001b[39mUpdated\u001b[14G\u001b[1mSPEC.md\u001b[22G\u001b[22m\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m(+1 -0)\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m\u001b[2m 90 \u001b[22m - Transfer count is the true minimum: `k − m`, where `k` = members with non-zero balance and `m` = maximum number of disjoint zero-sum subsets of tho\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m    \u001b[22m se balances. Computed with a bitmask DP over subsets (O(2^k · k)); within each zero-sum subset, transfers are produced by greedy debtor/creditor matc\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m    \u001b[22m hing (exactly `|subset| − 1` transfers).\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m 91 \u001b[22m - Practical limit: `k ≤ 20` uses the exact DP. If `k > 20` (only possible in groups larger than 20), fall back to greedy matching over the whole grou\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m    \u001b[22m p (≤ `k − 1` transfers, n"]
[0.001, "o", "ot guaranteed minimal). Documented, not an error.\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m 92 \u001b[22m - Output is deterministic for the same data (ties broken by member join order).\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m 93 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m- Results are memoized in-process, keyed by the group's exact balance vector (`(memberId, cents)` in join order), LRU-bounded to 1024 entries. Any ch\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m    +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mange to a group's balances is a new key, so a stale result can never be served and no explicit invalidation is needed; repeated reads of an unchanged\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m    +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m group cost one balance query, not a recomputation.                                                                                                  \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[2m 94 \u001b[22m \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m 95 \u001b[22m ## Data Model (SQLite)\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m 96 \u001b[22m \r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m  ⎿  Allowed by auto mode classifier\r\u001b[2B\u001b[38;2;215;119;87m✢\u001b[3G\u001b[38;2;233;154;122mUndulating…\u001b[38;2;215;119;87m \u001b[38;2;153;153;153m(24"]
