[0.000, "o", "\u001b[22m 1b[7B\\u001b[38;2;235;159;127mUndulating…\\u001b[39m\\u001b[40;1H\\u001b[38;3H\\u001b[?25h\\u001b[?2026l\"]\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m 11803 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m[0.034, \"o\", \"\\u001b[?2026h\\u001b[?25l\\u001b[H\\r\\u001b[33B\\u001b[38;2;215;119;87m✶\\u001b[39m\\u001b[40;1H\\u001b[38;3H\\u001b[?25h\\u001b[?2026l\"]    \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m 11804 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m[0.118, \"o\", \"\\u001b[?2026h\\u001b[?25l\\u001b[H\\r\\u001b[33B\\u001b[38;2;215;119;87m✻\\u001b[3G\\u001b[38;2;233;154;122mUndulating…\\u001b[28G\\u001b[38;\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m       +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m2;153;153;153m6\\u001b[39m\\u001b[40;1H\\u001b[38;3H\\u001b[?25h\\u001b[?2026l\"]                                                                       \r\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m  ⎿  \u001b[39mUpdated\u001b[14G\u001b[1mREADME.md\u001b[24G\u001b[22m\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m(+1 -1)\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m\u001b[2m 66 \u001b[22m \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m 67 \u001b[22m The minimum number of transfers is `k − g`, where `k` is the number of members with a non-zero balance and `g` is the largest num"]
[0.001, "o", "ber of disjoint grou\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m    \u001b[22m ps whose balances each sum to zero (each such group settles internally in `size − 1` transfers). This is computed exactly over all subsets when `k ≤ \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m    \u001b[22m 20`; above that it falls back to in-order debtor/creditor matching, which still clears every debt exactly but may use more than the minimum (at most \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m    \u001b[22m `k − 1` transfers).\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m 68 \u001b[22m \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;220;90;90m\u001b[48;2;61;1;0m 69 -\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mCost at the exact limit (20 non-zero balances) is roughly 0.15 s CPU and 20 MB peak memory per call; groups are capped at 50 members (`409 GROUP_FULL\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;220;90;90m    -\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m`).                                                                                                                                                  \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m 69 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mCost at the exact limit (20 non-zero balances) is roughly 0.15 s CPU and 20 MB peak memory to compute; groups are"]
[0.001, "o", " capped at 50 members (`409 GROUP_FU\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m    +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mLL`). Results are memoized in-process on the group's exact balances (LRU, 1024 entries), so repeat requests for an unchanged group take ~1 ms, and an\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m    +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242my new expense or member changes the key, so results are never stale.                                                                                 \r\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m  ⎿  \u001b[39mUpdated\u001b[14G\u001b[1mtasks/todo.md\u001b[28G\u001b[22m\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m(+1 -1)\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m\u001b[2m 196 \u001b[22m - [ ] Unicode case-insensitive member names (`COLLATE NOCASE` is ASCII-only)\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m 197 \u001b[22m - [ ] SQLite WAL / busy timeout for concurrent writes\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m 198 \u001b[22m - [ ] `max_length` on `splitBetween`\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;220;90;90m\u001b[48;2;61;1;0m 199 -\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m- [ ] Cache settle-up per group (each call still costs up to ~0.15 s / 20 MB)                                                                       \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;"]
[0.002, "o", "2;80;200;80m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m 199 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m- [x] Cache settle-up per group: memoized on the exact balance vector (LRU 1024), so no invalidation is needed; HTTP timing at 20 non-zero balances:\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m     +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m cold 152 ms → warm 1 ms                                                                                                                            \r\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m  ⎿  Allowed by auto mode classifier\r\u001b[2B\u001b[38;2;215;119;87m✽\u001b[3G\u001b[38;2;228;144;112mUndulating…\u001b[38;2;215;119;87m \u001b[38;2;153;153;153m(1m 7s · ↓\u001b[26G5.6k tokens)\r\u001b[1B  ⎿  Tip: Use /btw to ask a quick side question without interrupting Claude's current work\u001b[39m\u001b[40;1H\u001b[38;3H\u001b[?25h\u001b[?2026l"]
