[0.003, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\u001b[6G\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m\u001b[2m 196 \u001b[22m - [ ] Unicode case-insensitive member names (`COLLATE NOCASE` is ASCII-only)\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m\u001b[2m 197 \u001b[22m - [ ] SQLite WAL / busy timeout for concurrent writes\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m\u001b[2m 198 \u001b[22m - [ ] `max_length` on `splitBetween`\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B     \u001b[38;2;220;90;90m\u001b[48;2;61;1;0m 199 -\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m- [ ] Cache settle-up per group (each call still costs up to ~0.15 s / 20 MB)                                                                       \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m 199 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m- [x] Cache settle-up per group: memoized on the exact balance vector (LRU 1024), so no invalidation is needed; HTTP timing at 20 non-zero balances:\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m     +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m cold 152 ms → warm 1 ms                                                                                                                            \r\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m  ⎿  Allowed by auto mode classifi"]
[0.003, "o", "er\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;255;255;255m⏺\u001b[3G\u001b[39mI've added settle-up caching and committed it as \u001b[38;2;177;185;249m72f6fba\u001b[39m. On a 20-member group where everyone has a non-zero balance, the first settle-up request takes 152 ms\u001b[162Gand\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Brepeat requests take about 1 ms. All 142 tests pass, coverage is still 100%, and mypy and ruff are clean.\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[1mHow it works:\r\u001b[1B\u001b[22m \u001b[3G- S\u001b[7Gttle-up results are cached in me\u001b[40Gory, keyed by the group's\u001b[66Gexact \u001b[73Galances (each m\u001b[89Gmber ID\u001b[97Gwith their balance in cents). In prac\u001b[135Gice that's one entry per group,\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B  b\u001b[7Gcaus\u001b[12G m\u001b[15Gmber IDs\u001b[24Gbelong to only one group.\u001b[50G\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B-\u001b[5GThe\u001b[9Ganswer\u001b[16Gdepends\u001b[24Gonly\u001b[29Gon\u001b[32Gthose\u001b[38Gbalances.\u001b[48GSo\u001b[51Gwhen\u001b[56Ga\u001b[58Gnew\u001b[62Gexpense\u001b[70Gor\u001b[73Gmember\u001b[80Gchanges\u001b[88Gthem,\u001b[94Gthe\u001b[98Gnext\u001b[103Grequest\u001b[111Gmisses\u001b[118Gthe\u001b[122Gcache\u001b[128Gand\u001b[132Grecomputes,\u001b[144Gand\u001b[148Gan\u001b[151Goutdated\u001b[160Gresult\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B  can never be\u001b[18Greturned.\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1BNo"]
[0.001, "o", "\u001b[8Ghing need\u001b[18G clearing when data changes, an\u001b[51Gthe database \u001b[65Gchema didn't change. Each request still reads the balances from the database, which is chea\u001b[157G; only the\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1Bexpen\u001b[11Give calculation is skipped.\u001b[39G\u001b[K\r\u001b[8C\u001b[1Bcach\u001b[14G holds up\u001b[24Gto 1,024 groups and drops the le\u001b[57Gst recently used beyond that.\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B-\u001b[5GI add\u001b[11Gd this\u001b[19Gule to the\u001b[30Gspec\u001b[35Gbefore\u001b[42Gwriting\u001b[50Gthe\u001b[54Gcode.\u001b[60GThe\u001b[64GREADME\u001b[71Gand\u001b[75G\u001b[38;2;177;185;249mtasks/todo.md\u001b[89G\u001b[39mare\u001b[93Gupdated\u001b[101Gtoo.\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[1mTests added:\u001b[22m\u001b[K\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1BA repeat reque\u001b[20Gt for an unchanged group is \u001b[49Gerv\u001b[53Gd from\u001b[60Gthe cache, and the resul\u001b[85G matches\u001b[94Gthe\u001b[98Guncached\u001b[107Gcalculation.\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1BAfter an expense is add\u001b[29Gd to a cach\u001b[41Gd group,\u001b[50Gsettle-up\u001b[60Greturns the \u001b[73Gew figure (€10.00 owed becomes €6.00),\u001b[112Gnot\u001b[116Gthe\u001b[120Gold\u001b[124Gone.\r\u001b[2C\u001b[2B\u001b[1mLimits:\u001b[22m\u001b[K\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1BThe cache is per\u001b[22Gprocess. If you run several u\u001b[52Gicorn work\u001b[63Grs, each one"]
[0.001, "o", " computes its own copy\u001b[98Go\u001b[101Ge.\u001b[K\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1BI\u001b[7G several r\u001b[18Gqu\u001b[21Gst\u001b[25Gfor the s\u001b[35Gme unchanged group arrive before\u001b[72Gfirst one finishes, each of them does the full ca\u001b[122Gculation.\u001b[132GAfter\u001b[138Gthat\u001b[143Git's\u001b[148Gcomputed\u001b[157Gonce\u001b[162Gper\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1Bchange\u001b[12Gto\u001b[15Gthe\u001b[19Gbalances.\u001b[29GMaking\u001b[36Gsimultaneous\u001b[49Grequests\u001b[58Gshare\u001b[64Gone\u001b[68Gcalculation\u001b[80Gwould\u001b[86Gneed\u001b[91Ga\u001b[93Glock\u001b[98Gper\u001b[102Ggroup;\u001b[109GI\u001b[111Gcan\u001b[115Gadd\u001b[119Gthat\u001b[124Gif\u001b[127Gyou\u001b[131Gwant.\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m✻\u001b[3GBrewed for 1m 14s · done 6:20 PM\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2B\u001b[48;2;55;55;55m\u001b[38;2;80;80;80m❯ \u001b[38;2;153;153;153m/context\u001b[39m                                                                                                                                                            \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;215;119;87m✽\u001b[3GCrystallizi\u001b[38;2;235;159;127mng…\u001b[38;2;215;119;87m \u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[57C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m❯ \u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[38C\u001b[2B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m · esc to interrupt · "]
